# Progress — 2026-09-15: BigKinds xlsx → JSON mirrors

- Added `preprocess/bigkinds_to_json.py` (`python -m preprocess.bigkinds_to_json`):
  all 61 `data/raw/bigkinds/**/*.xlsx` → records-array `.json` beside each. Originals kept.
- All 19 original columns, original Korean names. No `bigkinds_schema.COLUMN_MAP`
  renaming — that belongs to `build_corpus.py`, this is a format-only mirror.
- `dtype=str` for every column, per the `bigkinds_schema` note that `뉴스 식별자`
  (`02100311.20210131095312001`) becomes a float without it.
- 998,020 rows total; 1,071.7 MB → 2,830.7 MB (2.764 GB on disk, 61 files).
- Verified twice: in-script reload, then an independent openpyxl `read_only` cell-by-cell
  diff that bypasses pandas. 61/61 OK.
- Found: 55 of 61 exports declare `<dimension ref="A1"/>` in `xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml`
  (2021:12, 2022:12, 2024:12, 2025:12, 2026:7); only the 6 2023 files are correct. openpyxl
  `read_only` trusts it and yields 1 row × 1 col; needs `ws.reset_dimensions()`.
  `build_corpus.py` uses plain `pd.read_excel` (not read_only) so it is unaffected.
- `data/raw/bigkinds/*` is gitignored; nothing new is tracked.

